  'MS-051', 'maths-standard', 'Maths_Standard', 'Some Applications of Trigonometry',
  9, 'Two elevation angles', NULL,
  'A tower is observed from two points on the same straight line on one side of its base. Their angles of elevation are 60° and 30°. The points are 260 m apart. Find the height.', '130√3 m.', 'Let the nearer distance be x and height H. H=x√3=(x+260)/√3. Hence 3x=x+260, giving x=130 and H=130√3.',
  3, 'NCERT Mathematics, Chapter 9: Some Applications of Trigonometry', 'Original worked solution using textbook methods',
  '["elevation","tower"]'::jsonb, 106, 96,
  '[2017,2018,2019,2020,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026]'::jsonb, TRUE, 'Very high',
