  'Establish that 1 + √2 is irrational.', 'Assume it is rational. Subtracting the integer 1 would make √2 rational, which contradicts its irrationality.', 'For √2, suppose √2=u/v with coprime integers and v non-zero. Then u²=2v² implies 2 divides u and subsequently v. This contradicts coprimality. A rational integer added to an irrational number cannot make the sum rational.',
