  'EC-065', 'english-communicative', 'English_Communicative', 'Factual descriptions',
  1, 'Factual descriptions', NULL,
  'Write a factual description of a reading-room volunteer in a maximum of 100 words. Use these details: short dark hair; blue identity badge; speaks calmly; arranges returned books; assists new readers. Do not invent a personal history or unsupported opinions.', 'The reading-room volunteer has short dark hair and wears a blue identity badge. She speaks calmly when assisting new readers. Her duties include arranging returned books so that visitors can find them. These visible features and tasks identify her role in the room. The description does not assume an age, qualification or personal history that has not been supplied.', 'Organise supplied visible/functional details into a coherent description. Neutral accuracy matters more than extravagant praise or invented biography.',
