  'You are Riya Sen of 14 Lake Road, Navapur. Write a formal letter to the Municipal Services Officer about mixed waste around the market. Use these facts: Food waste and recyclable material are left together in open heaps. Request labelled collection points, regular removal and awareness messages. Use a maximum of 120 words.', '14 Lake Road, Navapur
13/10/2026
Municipal Officer, Navapur
Subject: Request for action
Sir/Madam,
I am writing about mixed waste around the market. Food waste and recyclable material are left together in open heaps. This affects vendors and shoppers and calls for a practical response. I request labelled collection points, regular removal and awareness messages. Please inspect the concern and consult users before finalising the action. A clear timeline and a named contact would help us follow progress and report any remaining problems. We are willing to share observations and cooperate with a workable solution. Kindly acknowledge this request and inform us of the proposed steps. Timely action would improve daily routines.
Yours faithfully,
Riya Sen', 'Use sender/recipient details, a clear subject, polite formal tone, the supplied concern, specific requested action and an appropriate closing. This is an original model; equivalent relevant responses are acceptable.',
