(
  'EC-131', 'english-communicative', 'English_Communicative', 'Articles',
  1, 'Articles', NULL,
  'Write an article titled Balanced screen habits for a school magazine in a maximum of 150 words. Develop these cues: Use purposeful study periods, reduce non-essential interruptions, protect sleep and preserve offline activity.', 'Balanced screen habits
By Riya Sen
Balanced screen habits deserves attention in our everyday choices. Use purposeful study periods, reduce non-essential interruptions, protect sleep and preserve offline activity. These actions become useful when they are turned into regular, practical habits rather than treated as a one-day promise. Students can begin with a small achievable change, discuss it with peers and review whether it actually helps. Families and schools can support the effort by setting a good example and making participation easier. Clear information and respectful discussion are more useful than blame or exaggerated claims. Progress may be gradual, but shared responsibility makes it more sustainable. The next step is to choose one relevant action and follow it consistently.', 'Give a title/byline, develop the supplied theme through connected reasoning, offer relevant actions and conclude coherently. This original model is one acceptable response, not a memorisation requirement.',
  8, 'Original passage/response; competency alignment: CBSE Interact in English skills and current English Communicative syllabus', 'Original language-skill material; not copied textbook content',
  '["article","magazine"]'::jsonb, 195, 84.2,
  '[2017,2019,2024,2025,2026]'::jsonb, TRUE, 'High',
  131, 1, TRUE, FALSE
),
